00:22:51.290 --> 00:22:52.640
The story of Jesus's birth.

00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:56.210
And I think it's just an interesting thing

00:22:56.210 --> 00:22:58.020
in our culture in America.

00:22:58.020 --> 00:22:59.860
I guess this happens in other places

00:22:59.860 --> 00:23:03.300
but there's like this longstanding thing

00:23:03.300 --> 00:23:04.210
that happens between,

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:05.962
like there's the Merry Christmas people

00:23:05.962 --> 00:23:07.756
and there's the happy holidays people

00:23:07.756 --> 00:23:09.730
and there's like this
battle line that's drawn

00:23:09.730 --> 00:23:11.530
and like people get mad at Starbucks

00:23:11.530 --> 00:23:14.490
if they don't say Merry
Christmas or whatever, right?

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:18.200
And this is a relatively
recent sort of cultural battle

00:23:18.200 --> 00:23:23.200
but I remember what I
can relate to about this

00:23:24.190 --> 00:23:29.190
is I remember as a Christian and listen,

00:23:29.200 --> 00:23:30.350
a Christian who was like working

00:23:30.350 --> 00:23:31.740
for a Christian organization full-time,

00:23:31.740 --> 00:23:33.090
like taking it very seriously.

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:36.810
I always thought that this
little cultural infighting

00:23:36.810 --> 00:23:38.690
about the whole Merry Christmas thing,

00:23:38.690 --> 00:23:40.830
I was like why are y'all
getting so upset about this?

00:23:40.830 --> 00:23:41.740
Yeah, I mean-

00:23:41.740 --> 00:23:42.893
I've never related to it.

00:23:42.893 --> 00:23:45.310
I think another way that
we might've put it was,

00:23:45.310 --> 00:23:47.447
'cause I agree that was
my assessment at the time,

00:23:47.447 --> 00:23:49.120
was like this is not a good look.

00:23:49.120 --> 00:23:50.540
This is not the-

00:23:50.540 --> 00:23:53.520
This is not the battle
that we should be fighting.

00:23:53.520 --> 00:23:55.835
What is your desired
outcome from this battle?

00:23:55.835 --> 00:23:58.550
That some atheist somewhere
would say yes, you're right.

00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:00.069
Merry Christmas.

00:24:00.069 --> 00:24:01.962
Is that what we're trying to accomplish?

00:24:01.962 --> 00:24:05.610
It felt like a turf war,
like protecting your turf

00:24:05.610 --> 00:24:10.610
and again, I was like very
much on board for Jesus

00:24:11.500 --> 00:24:13.140
is the reason for the season.

00:24:13.140 --> 00:24:14.420
'Cause it rhymes?

00:24:14.420 --> 00:24:16.790
It looks great in a store window.

00:24:16.790 --> 00:24:19.340
Yeah, a couple of months ago,

00:24:19.340 --> 00:24:21.980
we were we were driving past this,

00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:24.845
all my family was in the
car and we drove past,

00:24:24.845 --> 00:24:26.750
I guess it was October

00:24:26.750 --> 00:24:31.300
and on automobile lot
and they got the showroom

00:24:31.300 --> 00:24:32.680
with like the big glass windows

00:24:32.680 --> 00:24:35.380
and they paint all their
windshields with prices

00:24:35.380 --> 00:24:40.360
but they painted their
showroom windows huge

00:24:40.360 --> 00:24:41.420
across all the windows.

00:24:41.420 --> 00:24:46.160
Like if you had really
take the time to back up

00:24:46.160 --> 00:24:47.780
or really take in the whole thing,

00:24:47.780 --> 00:24:49.380
across the whole thing, it said

00:24:49.380 --> 00:24:51.960
Jesus is the reason for the season

00:24:51.960 --> 00:24:53.130
and then it was October.

00:24:53.130 --> 00:24:54.700
They had never taken it down.

00:24:54.700 --> 00:24:55.590
So I'm like-

00:24:55.590 --> 00:24:56.423
Well.

00:24:56.423 --> 00:24:58.750
Well, kids you know what? It's fall.

00:24:58.750 --> 00:24:59.583
Jesus is the reason for the season.

00:24:59.583 --> 00:25:00.700
Jesus is the reason for fall.

00:25:00.700 --> 00:25:01.600
And technically,

00:25:01.600 --> 00:25:02.723
that's true.
It maybe right.

00:25:02.723 --> 00:25:04.633
I mean from that perspective.

00:25:06.060 --> 00:25:09.490
So yeah, so we didn't really
get in on that bandwagon

00:25:09.490 --> 00:25:11.176
and to me, it felt silly

00:25:11.176 --> 00:25:13.730
when I saw Christians
getting really concerned

00:25:13.730 --> 00:25:15.090
about that particular issue.

00:25:15.090 --> 00:25:17.203
Even though for us personally,

00:25:18.363 --> 00:25:23.363
Jesus was absolutely
the center of Christmas,

00:25:23.520 --> 00:25:25.630
which was the main holiday

00:25:25.630 --> 00:25:27.940
that we were personally celebrating.

00:25:27.940 --> 00:25:30.129
Yeah, and the way that I relate to-

00:25:30.129 --> 00:25:32.493
There are other holidays that
are happening around then

00:25:32.493 --> 00:25:35.470
that other people celebrate, you know?

00:25:35.470 --> 00:25:38.670
So just say happy holidays
just to acknowledge

00:25:38.670 --> 00:25:41.804
that other people are
celebrating other holidays

00:25:41.804 --> 00:25:43.290
is not a bad thing.

00:25:43.290 --> 00:25:45.170
That's just called being considerate.

00:25:45.170 --> 00:25:47.557
Right, it seems very Christian, actually.

00:25:47.557 --> 00:25:49.930
So I just never got that.

00:25:49.930 --> 00:25:51.191
I'm glad.

00:25:51.191 --> 00:25:52.340
I mean there's lots of things I'm like

00:25:52.340 --> 00:25:53.530
I wish I would've done it differently

00:25:53.530 --> 00:25:56.300
but I never fought that fight.

00:25:56.300 --> 00:25:57.806
Yeah, but the thing that-

00:25:57.806 --> 00:26:00.010
I never insisted that
somebody else celebrate

00:26:00.010 --> 00:26:01.300
something that I'm celebrating.

00:26:01.300 --> 00:26:03.940
Right, right but the
thing that I can relate to

00:26:03.940 --> 00:26:07.810
when it comes to this
maybe holding Christmas

00:26:07.810 --> 00:26:09.100
in a precious way

00:26:10.330 --> 00:26:14.350
is the secular treatment of Christmas,

00:26:14.350 --> 00:26:15.240
just traditionally, right?

00:26:15.240 --> 00:26:19.440
So you've got like okay,
you've got Charles Dickens

00:26:19.440 --> 00:26:20.480
as an example, right?

00:26:20.480 --> 00:26:22.710
So you've got "A Christmas Carol"

00:26:22.710 --> 00:26:24.930
or really anything that centers

00:26:24.930 --> 00:26:27.350
around the spirit of Christmas

00:26:27.350 --> 00:26:30.140
as it relates to anything
other than Jesus.

00:26:30.140 --> 00:26:33.650
So you've got Santa and gift-giving and-

00:26:33.650 --> 00:26:37.030
Well, gift-giving, you
could say that the tree,

00:26:37.030 --> 00:26:39.090
some people say the tree is Pagan,

00:26:39.090 --> 00:26:41.070
some people say the tree is Christian,

00:26:41.070 --> 00:26:41.903
some people say gift-giving-

00:26:41.903 --> 00:26:44.100
You can come and do all these things

00:26:44.100 --> 00:26:46.240
for your individual purposes

00:26:46.240 --> 00:26:47.494
but what I'm saying is that like,

00:26:47.494 --> 00:26:51.620
I wasn't one of these
anti-Santa Christians either

00:26:51.620 --> 00:26:56.050
and not in like a Santa
is just Satan rearranged

00:26:56.050 --> 00:26:57.500
in the same letters, right?

00:26:57.500 --> 00:26:58.980
Like there are Christians who think that

00:26:58.980 --> 00:27:01.390
and think that Santa is
this secular distraction.

00:27:01.390 --> 00:27:02.350
I didn't think that either

00:27:02.350 --> 00:27:05.593
but what I did think is when
I would see a Christmas movie,

00:27:06.470 --> 00:27:09.270
let's say "Elf" as an
example, your favorite movie.

00:27:09.270 --> 00:27:10.103
Best movie ever.

00:27:10.103 --> 00:27:12.340
I could appreciate how
awesome of a movie it is,

00:27:12.340 --> 00:27:14.520
not necessarily my
favorite even in my top 10

00:27:14.520 --> 00:27:17.050
but a very solid Christmas movie.

00:27:17.050 --> 00:27:19.330
I could appreciate it and appreciate

00:27:19.330 --> 00:27:24.280
all the good principles that
it kinda, that it reinforced

00:27:24.280 --> 00:27:27.080
in the spirit of Christmas
but as a Christian,

00:27:27.080 --> 00:27:28.350
I would kinda stand aside

00:27:28.350 --> 00:27:31.440
and say yeah, that's a real nice story

00:27:31.440 --> 00:27:32.760
but you guys do know

00:27:32.760 --> 00:27:34.610
that Jesus is the reason for the season,

00:27:34.610 --> 00:27:35.880
that the whole point of this holiday

00:27:35.880 --> 00:27:37.703
is to celebrate the fact
that God became a human,

00:27:37.703 --> 00:27:40.200
came down on our level and gave us a way

00:27:40.200 --> 00:27:41.250
to be reconciled to him.

00:27:41.250 --> 00:27:42.730
You do understand that's what's it about.

00:27:42.730 --> 00:27:44.350
Well, and it's one thing to imply it

00:27:44.350 --> 00:27:47.480
in all of the Hollywood Christmas movies

00:27:47.480 --> 00:27:50.920
but I mean, in a lot of
times, it's blatantly stated

00:27:50.920 --> 00:27:54.300
that the reason for the season

00:27:54.300 --> 00:27:56.020
or they may put it in different terms

00:27:56.020 --> 00:27:57.100
but they'll blatantly say

00:27:57.100 --> 00:28:00.360
that like the spirit
of Christmas is family.

00:28:00.360 --> 00:28:02.800
It's like good tidings.

00:28:02.800 --> 00:28:03.633
Right.

00:28:03.633 --> 00:28:08.530
It's I'll be home for Christmas,
it's getting together.

00:28:08.530 --> 00:28:10.940
It's that type of stuff.

00:28:10.940 --> 00:28:13.704
And I didn't want people
to change their movies.

00:28:13.704 --> 00:28:15.211
I wasn't thinking like,

00:28:15.211 --> 00:28:19.654
"Elf" would have been a
whole lot better if like,

00:28:19.654 --> 00:28:21.160
if the, what's the elf's name?

00:28:21.160 --> 00:28:22.460
You should know this.

00:28:22.460 --> 00:28:23.610
Will Ferrell.

00:28:23.610 --> 00:28:24.760
Well, what's his name in the movie?

00:28:24.760 --> 00:28:25.593
Buddy.

00:28:25.593 --> 00:28:29.020
If Buddy would have become a
Christian during the movie,

00:28:29.020 --> 00:28:30.240
like I'm not talking about like,

00:28:30.240 --> 00:28:33.920
I'm not saying I wanna have
like Kirk Cameron type movies.

00:28:33.920 --> 00:28:35.160
I wasn't into that.

00:28:35.160 --> 00:28:36.420
No, no, no, we hated those.

00:28:36.420 --> 00:28:37.253
We hated those.

00:28:37.253 --> 00:28:38.540
We hated those movies.

00:28:38.540 --> 00:28:39.950
We hated movies that
were explicitly Christian

00:28:39.950 --> 00:28:41.730
and had but-

00:28:41.730 --> 00:28:43.630
Because they weren't artful.

00:28:43.630 --> 00:28:44.463
Yeah.

00:28:44.463 --> 00:28:45.840
Most, all of them.
Again, it felt like

00:28:45.840 --> 00:28:48.733
it was for the audience but anyway,

00:28:49.790 --> 00:28:52.200
or it was preaching to
the choir, whatever.

00:28:52.200 --> 00:28:55.280
But I still had this sort
of judgment in my mind

00:28:55.280 --> 00:28:57.890
that was like, yeah,
you guys almost get it

00:28:57.890 --> 00:28:59.870
but you don't really get it.

00:28:59.870 --> 00:29:03.130
You've created all this
holiday accoutrement

00:29:03.130 --> 00:29:06.610
around Christmas in order
to make it seem meaningful

00:29:06.610 --> 00:29:09.030
but you've missed the heart of it

00:29:09.030 --> 00:29:12.170
which is this is about Jesus y'all.

00:29:12.170 --> 00:29:15.010
And so, it's all pointless, ultimately.

00:29:15.010 --> 00:29:17.860
If you're gonna miss the heart of it,

00:29:17.860 --> 00:29:20.700
then all this stuff around, it
really doesn't mean anything.

00:29:20.700 --> 00:29:24.540
I was very sensitive to putting my values

00:29:24.540 --> 00:29:27.940
and expectations onto other people

00:29:27.940 --> 00:29:31.020
that I didn't think I had
any realistic expectation

00:29:31.020 --> 00:29:33.193
that they will be interested in that.

00:29:34.200 --> 00:29:35.800
But I'll tell you what I did do.

00:29:37.360 --> 00:29:40.023
Yeah, I mean, as a kid,

00:29:41.410 --> 00:29:43.230
our evangelical upbringing

00:29:43.230 --> 00:29:46.300
was like the center point of our identity.

00:29:46.300 --> 00:29:47.860
I mean, and then

00:29:50.760 --> 00:29:52.860
I think for me, there had to be like

00:29:54.510 --> 00:29:56.290
looking down my nose at other people

00:29:56.290 --> 00:29:59.480
or just maybe feeling sorry for people

00:29:59.480 --> 00:30:02.607
who are just missing like the real point

00:30:05.920 --> 00:30:08.307
of what needs to be
celebrated at Christmas

00:30:08.307 --> 00:30:10.370
and what I'm experiencing and celebrating.

00:30:10.370 --> 00:30:12.350
It was more of a bless
their hearts kinda thing.

00:30:12.350 --> 00:30:15.700
Yeah, there was a depth in the experience

00:30:15.700 --> 00:30:18.920
that I was having that I felt like,

00:30:18.920 --> 00:30:23.920
by comparison, from my
evangelical perspective

00:30:24.300 --> 00:30:26.070
looking at other people, just thinking,

00:30:26.070 --> 00:30:29.600
okay, it's just a bit, it's a bit shallow.

00:30:29.600 --> 00:30:34.577
Yeah, I mean like family
and love and service

00:30:34.577 --> 00:30:36.233
and all these good things are,

00:30:37.650 --> 00:30:39.180
they're very meaningful things

00:30:39.180 --> 00:30:42.720
but they're not as meaningful as God

00:30:42.720 --> 00:30:46.430
coming to Earth, humbling
himself as a baby.

00:30:46.430 --> 00:30:50.140
Like that's tremendously inspirational

00:30:50.140 --> 00:30:52.883
and a lot of other things.

00:30:54.800 --> 00:30:57.270
And then when when
Christy and I got married

00:30:57.270 --> 00:30:59.260
and we started having kids,

00:30:59.260 --> 00:31:03.620
it's like, okay, now,
it's my opportunity to,

00:31:03.620 --> 00:31:07.240
I'm in charge of creating new traditions

00:31:07.240 --> 00:31:09.400
and finding the ways that
we're gonna keep Jesus

00:31:09.400 --> 00:31:14.400
at the center of our focus.

00:31:14.540 --> 00:31:18.453
And so one of the things
we did is we would,

00:31:20.272 --> 00:31:25.272
we made up our mind that we
were gonna always tell our kids

00:31:27.080 --> 00:31:30.570
that and maybe we need to put
a spoiler alert on this but-

00:31:30.570 --> 00:31:31.403
I don't-

00:31:31.403 --> 00:31:32.370
You know what I'm about to say.

00:31:32.370 --> 00:31:33.420
If there's somebody listening

00:31:33.420 --> 00:31:36.493
that you don't wanna
know certain things that-

00:31:36.493 --> 00:31:40.900
About the man, the
secular man of Christmas?

00:31:40.900 --> 00:31:41.733
Yeah.

00:31:41.733 --> 00:31:42.620
We're gonna reveal the truth

00:31:42.620 --> 00:31:43.810
about the secular man of Christmas

00:31:43.810 --> 00:31:44.780
so if you have a little ones

00:31:44.780 --> 00:31:47.120
who are listening in on this conversation

00:31:47.120 --> 00:31:50.130
and you want the miracle of
Christmas to remain alive,

00:31:50.130 --> 00:31:51.222
tune out right now.

00:31:51.222 --> 00:31:53.050
This what's happening right here

00:31:53.050 --> 00:31:56.190
was never a problem for
me because I decided.

00:31:56.190 --> 00:31:58.373
I think this was a Link decision.

00:31:59.482 --> 00:32:00.660
It's like, you know what,

00:32:00.660 --> 00:32:05.470
our kids are always gonna know
that Santa is just is fake

00:32:05.470 --> 00:32:06.887
but we're still gonna have,

00:32:06.887 --> 00:32:09.230
we're still gonna surprise
them with presents

00:32:10.590 --> 00:32:13.530
on Christmas morning that weren't
wrapped in under the tree.

00:32:13.530 --> 00:32:15.050
There's gonna be some unwrapped stuff

00:32:15.050 --> 00:32:17.250
that's gonna be there when
they run down the stairs

00:32:17.250 --> 00:32:19.220
and I still wanna have that scene

00:32:19.220 --> 00:32:21.640
because it's so exciting

00:32:21.640 --> 00:32:23.090
and I don't wanna take that away entirely.

00:32:23.090 --> 00:32:23.923
But when the weatherman

00:32:23.923 --> 00:32:26.500
is like we've spotted Santa on the radar.

00:32:26.500 --> 00:32:28.370
I'd be like, kids, that's BS.

00:32:28.370 --> 00:32:32.050
When Lily's five years
old, she never thought,

00:32:32.050 --> 00:32:33.690
there was never a point where she thought

00:32:33.690 --> 00:32:37.020
and she knew that she wasn't
supposed to tell other kids

00:32:37.020 --> 00:32:40.690
and unlike you who told me
way too late in my experience

00:32:40.690 --> 00:32:42.303
that Santa Claus was fake,

00:32:43.990 --> 00:32:47.245
she did not do that to her
friends at a young age.

00:32:47.245 --> 00:32:48.923
Well, the funny thing about this

00:32:48.923 --> 00:32:51.940
is that I never made a
decision one way or the other.

00:32:51.940 --> 00:32:55.020
I always, you know me,
I like making things up,

00:32:55.020 --> 00:32:56.620
making my kids believe
things that aren't true

00:32:56.620 --> 00:32:58.850
just for my own personal entertainment.

00:32:58.850 --> 00:33:02.020
And so Santa, it fits
the bill there, right?

00:33:02.020 --> 00:33:04.430
And so we would-

00:33:04.430 --> 00:33:06.220
Your Santa probably was real crazy.

00:33:06.220 --> 00:33:07.383
Well, the thing is is that-

00:33:07.383 --> 00:33:10.470
Like he's got three eyes but
one of them has an eye patch.

00:33:10.470 --> 00:33:11.660
But think about my kids though.

00:33:11.660 --> 00:33:14.300
My kids are just like me and I didn't,

00:33:14.300 --> 00:33:16.190
the reason I didn't think Santa was real

00:33:16.190 --> 00:33:18.430
when I was a kid wasn't
because an adult told me,

00:33:18.430 --> 00:33:19.388
it was because-

00:33:19.388 --> 00:33:20.490
Are you saying you're
smarter than me as a kid?

00:33:20.490 --> 00:33:23.020
Well, no, I think about
things in a different way,

00:33:23.020 --> 00:33:24.110
let's just say that.

00:33:24.110 --> 00:33:26.368
I was like this can't be real.

00:33:26.368 --> 00:33:28.950
I embraced the wonder and joy of life

00:33:28.950 --> 00:33:30.366
and I don't question it.

00:33:30.366 --> 00:33:31.860
And so my kids did the exact same thing.

00:33:31.860 --> 00:33:32.860
There was never a moment

00:33:32.860 --> 00:33:34.800
where I had to break a truth to them.

00:33:34.800 --> 00:33:37.790
It was more just like at
some point, at an early age,

00:33:37.790 --> 00:33:39.410
they were just like, "I
know Santa is not real.

00:33:39.410 --> 00:33:40.550
I know you're giving me these gifts."

00:33:40.550 --> 00:33:41.383
I had made a-

00:33:41.383 --> 00:33:42.720
But it's fun to play along.

00:33:42.720 --> 00:33:46.040
I'd made a decision to
actually proactively tell them

00:33:46.040 --> 00:33:49.742
and like burst the bubble
before it would hurt too bad.

00:33:49.742 --> 00:33:54.742
The reason why I actually felt really good

00:33:54.800 --> 00:33:58.030
about saying this is a protection from,

00:33:58.030 --> 00:34:01.020
even for my kids at their youngest age,

00:34:01.020 --> 00:34:03.000
I'm removing some of the temptation

00:34:03.000 --> 00:34:04.830
to focus on the wrong thing.

00:34:04.830 --> 00:34:08.010
It's like remember, we're
focusing on Jesus here.

00:34:08.010 --> 00:34:09.100
We can have the presents

00:34:09.100 --> 00:34:11.311
and the reason why we have the presents

00:34:11.311 --> 00:34:15.330
was because presents were brought to Jesus

00:34:15.330 --> 00:34:20.330
because people knew that
he was God incarnate

00:34:20.340 --> 00:34:23.480
and they were they came
to worship him as a king

00:34:23.480 --> 00:34:24.960
and they gave him gifts.

00:34:24.960 --> 00:34:29.180
And so, you just try to couch everything

00:34:30.760 --> 00:34:32.470
through the lens of Jesus, right?

00:34:32.470 --> 00:34:34.310
That's a Christmas movie for Kirk Cameron.

00:34:34.310 --> 00:34:37.360
Right, through the lens of Jesus.

00:34:37.360 --> 00:34:39.190
And I felt good about that.

00:34:39.190 --> 00:34:43.608
Now, I don't feel bad
about it now but I just,

00:34:43.608 --> 00:34:46.710
I was kind of a stickler

00:34:46.710 --> 00:34:50.100
but I remember feeling like
this is something tangible

00:34:50.100 --> 00:34:54.100
that I've done that impacts
my family's ability to focus

00:34:54.100 --> 00:34:55.450
on what matters most.

00:34:55.450 --> 00:34:56.283
Well, and some people-

00:34:56.283 --> 00:34:58.290
And I think that that was my role.

00:34:58.290 --> 00:35:01.060
And some people might
say just another reason

00:35:01.060 --> 00:35:02.883
if this is your perspective.

00:35:04.660 --> 00:35:07.210
Another reason to clarify
the fact that Santa

00:35:07.210 --> 00:35:09.840
is a made up thing is
because you don't want it

00:35:09.840 --> 00:35:10.700
to be like, all right,

00:35:10.700 --> 00:35:13.970
there's two things that are true, child.

00:35:13.970 --> 00:35:17.500
Jesus is God's son and God in the flesh

00:35:17.500 --> 00:35:18.990
is the Christmas story

00:35:18.990 --> 00:35:21.330
but also, there's this
dude named Saint Nicholas

00:35:21.330 --> 00:35:24.390
who comes and flies
around, hauled by reindeer

00:35:24.390 --> 00:35:25.223
and gives you presents.

00:35:25.223 --> 00:35:26.056
Flying reindeer and
comes down your chimney.

00:35:26.056 --> 00:35:28.160
At some point, I'm gonna
break the news to you

00:35:28.160 --> 00:35:30.770
that one of these two things is not real.

00:35:30.770 --> 00:35:31.790
And the way I'm gonna do it

00:35:31.790 --> 00:35:34.370
is by saying one of these
is not real, you choose.

00:35:34.370 --> 00:35:35.410
Right, yeah.

00:35:35.410 --> 00:35:36.243
No, but you don't-

00:35:36.243 --> 00:35:39.000
Yeah, and so for, I think,
for some Christians,

00:35:39.000 --> 00:35:44.000
it's like hey, let's
tell our kids the truth,

00:35:44.510 --> 00:35:47.210
and again, this is the truth
according to a Christian,

00:35:48.180 --> 00:35:49.210
that hey, this story is real

00:35:49.210 --> 00:35:51.960
and this story is sort of
the secular cultural story

00:35:51.960 --> 00:35:53.930
that we tell ourselves
with sort of a fairytale

00:35:53.930 --> 00:35:56.270
like the like the Tooth Fairy,

00:35:56.270 --> 00:35:57.670
whatever Easter Bunny, you know?

00:35:57.670 --> 00:35:59.930
And they never believed the Easter Bunny

00:35:59.930 --> 00:36:01.250
or the Tooth Fairy really either

00:36:01.250 --> 00:36:02.895
for kind of the same reason.

00:36:02.895 --> 00:36:04.089
Easter Bunny is-

00:36:04.089 --> 00:36:06.153
I have this principle like you know what,

00:36:06.153 --> 00:36:08.110
I don't wanna have to break it to my kids

00:36:08.110 --> 00:36:09.810
that I was lying to 'em.

00:36:09.810 --> 00:36:11.931
I don't know that that's
how kids but is say-

00:36:11.931 --> 00:36:13.880
I never went there 'cause I
lie to my kids all the time

00:36:13.880 --> 00:36:17.850
but the Easter Bunny is
the worst holiday mascot

00:36:17.850 --> 00:36:20.800
because what does the Easter Bunny do?

00:36:20.800 --> 00:36:22.533
I mean the Tooth Fairy
has a very specific thing.

00:36:22.533 --> 00:36:25.267
It's a transactional relationship.

00:36:25.267 --> 00:36:28.440
You give him the tooth,
he gives you money.

00:36:28.440 --> 00:36:29.830
I understand how that works.

00:36:29.830 --> 00:36:30.840
I know when it happens.

00:36:30.840 --> 00:36:32.980
Are you picturing The Rock or something?

00:36:32.980 --> 00:36:33.910
You're saying he.

00:36:33.910 --> 00:36:36.240
Well, I'm saying he because
I played the Tooth Fairy

00:36:36.240 --> 00:36:40.280
in a video I'm very proud of.

00:36:40.280 --> 00:36:42.010
Do you remember that video that we made?

00:36:42.010 --> 00:36:42.843
I can't remember what it's called.

00:36:42.843 --> 00:36:43.676
Spot the differences?

00:36:43.676 --> 00:36:45.460
Spot the differences, whatever.

00:36:45.460 --> 00:36:46.763
But the Easter Bunny,

00:36:47.810 --> 00:36:50.811
no one says, hey, let's go
outside and find the eggs

00:36:50.811 --> 00:36:52.509
that the Easter Bunny hid.

00:36:52.509 --> 00:36:54.760
We do away with that mirage.

00:36:54.760 --> 00:36:56.423
We say no, the parents are going outside.

00:36:56.423 --> 00:36:59.720
What is the role of the Easter Bunny?

00:36:59.720 --> 00:37:02.460
I think to be eating his
chocolate, I don't know.

00:37:02.460 --> 00:37:06.040
Yeah, it's a weak ass,
weak ass holiday mascot.

00:37:06.040 --> 00:37:08.540
I will say there was another factor

00:37:08.540 --> 00:37:10.920
in saying that Santa Claus wasn't real

00:37:10.920 --> 00:37:12.180
but they still got the gifts

00:37:12.180 --> 00:37:15.130
because then I could take full
credit for all of the gifts.

00:37:16.760 --> 00:37:17.593
I understand that.

00:37:17.593 --> 00:37:19.492
I think that was an ulterior
motive on my behalf.

00:37:19.492 --> 00:37:23.950
But yeah, there was this, I mean I was,

00:37:23.950 --> 00:37:25.830
we had so many family to visit

00:37:25.830 --> 00:37:27.461
that We didn't go to the
Christmas Eve service.

00:37:27.461 --> 00:37:31.320
We didn't actually have a lot of like

00:37:31.320 --> 00:37:36.200
Christmas time traditions
but we did have some,

00:37:36.200 --> 00:37:40.300
like we would read like
from the children's Bible

00:37:40.300 --> 00:37:43.610
like the Christmas story from a young age.

00:37:43.610 --> 00:37:45.570
I've got this video of Lily

00:37:48.000 --> 00:37:50.149
before she could read,

00:37:50.149 --> 00:37:54.040
we had read it to her so
much that she had memorized

00:37:54.040 --> 00:37:57.050
the Christmas story based on
this children's picture book

00:37:57.050 --> 00:37:58.720
and it's cutest thing

00:37:58.720 --> 00:38:00.610
because she would act like she's reading

00:38:00.610 --> 00:38:05.070
but she just memorized
everything that we said per page.

00:38:05.070 --> 00:38:09.180
And it felt good to know
that one of the first things

00:38:09.180 --> 00:38:12.870
she memorized was the story

00:38:12.870 --> 00:38:17.040
of Jesus humbling himself
and coming to Earth

00:38:17.040 --> 00:38:19.913
in order to be her savior.

00:38:21.682 --> 00:38:23.463
I just felt like I was,

00:38:24.660 --> 00:38:27.870
okay, I was like this is my job as dad

00:38:27.870 --> 00:38:32.870
and Christy's job as mom is
to instill this knowledge

00:38:34.590 --> 00:38:39.590
in her at a young age to where
she knows that God loves her

00:38:40.160 --> 00:38:43.870
and cares about her and
went to great lengths

00:38:43.870 --> 00:38:46.070
to not only demonstrate that

00:38:46.070 --> 00:38:49.660
but to make that relationship possible.

00:38:49.660 --> 00:38:53.040
So it felt really good and
it was it was validating

00:38:53.040 --> 00:38:58.040
that we've got this system,
I've got this belief system

00:38:58.260 --> 00:39:02.123
that I'm all in with and I'm very,

00:39:04.010 --> 00:39:05.816
every benefit associated with it.

00:39:05.816 --> 00:39:08.760
I felt like I was, at the time,

00:39:08.760 --> 00:39:10.800
that I was only experiencing the benefits.

00:39:10.800 --> 00:39:12.790
I think I've processed in my other story

00:39:12.790 --> 00:39:15.940
that like there there's
another side to it for me

00:39:15.940 --> 00:39:19.350
but at Christmas time, it felt good.

00:39:19.350 --> 00:39:21.790
It's like okay, we're not
losing sight of the point.

00:39:21.790 --> 00:39:22.623
Yeah.

00:39:25.190 --> 00:39:29.220
Most of our touch points
related to church.

00:39:29.220 --> 00:39:31.710
We were very involved in our church.

00:39:31.710 --> 00:39:33.040
You were very involved
in your church as well

00:39:33.040 --> 00:39:34.910
but during Christmas, we
were very involved in church

00:39:34.910 --> 00:39:38.540
including like being
involved in the program

00:39:38.540 --> 00:39:41.470
to the point where every year, Jesus,

00:39:41.470 --> 00:39:45.813
Jessie, my wife, would put would
play Mary in this like play

00:39:45.813 --> 00:39:48.660
and I think maybe for
the first year she did it

00:39:48.660 --> 00:39:51.706
or one year she did it,
like Locke was Jesus

00:39:51.706 --> 00:39:54.510
but other years, it was
other people's babies,

00:39:54.510 --> 00:39:55.670
like a real baby.

00:39:55.670 --> 00:39:56.920
She would sing.

00:39:56.920 --> 00:39:57.753
Ah.

00:39:57.753 --> 00:40:00.290
Like, she's like this
one woman show as Mary.

00:40:00.290 --> 00:40:03.305
And you'd light candles and
it would be a big moment.

00:40:03.305 --> 00:40:06.200
The Advent and then there was that album,

00:40:06.200 --> 00:40:07.347
that dude, what is his name?

00:40:07.347 --> 00:40:11.160
Is it Andrew Peterson? Is that his name?

00:40:11.160 --> 00:40:12.580
I don't know if that's the-

00:40:12.580 --> 00:40:13.413
I don't know.

00:40:13.413 --> 00:40:14.360
I don't know if,

00:40:14.360 --> 00:40:15.370
there's this guy.

00:40:15.370 --> 00:40:20.370
He's the Christian musician
who came out with the album

00:40:20.560 --> 00:40:24.053
that has become the all the
songs that Christians play.

00:40:25.040 --> 00:40:28.480
It's been like 15 years
ago and it's just like...

00:40:31.050 --> 00:40:33.310
It's not "Mary, Did You
Know?", that's the old school.

00:40:33.310 --> 00:40:38.310
This is like it's the one
about like Mary in the...

00:40:38.460 --> 00:40:39.950
The whole album is a Christmas album

00:40:39.950 --> 00:40:41.260
and it's the one where like all the things

00:40:41.260 --> 00:40:42.710
that people singing and
evangelical churches come from.

00:40:42.710 --> 00:40:44.710
And I think this dude's name is Peterson.

00:40:44.710 --> 00:40:47.070
And you know these songs for 100% sure

00:40:47.070 --> 00:40:48.930
'cause you were a music
leader at your church.

00:40:48.930 --> 00:40:51.656
You just didn't maybe make
the connection to the album.

00:40:51.656 --> 00:40:52.989
I was the hip.

00:40:54.010 --> 00:40:54.843
I assume they're still,

00:40:54.843 --> 00:40:55.676
I know they're still playing them

00:40:55.676 --> 00:40:57.220
because when I went to
a Christmas Eve service

00:40:57.220 --> 00:41:00.430
at my old church like two years ago,

00:41:00.430 --> 00:41:01.263
it's still playing the same songs.

00:41:01.263 --> 00:41:02.120
So what is your point?

00:41:02.120 --> 00:41:03.030
I'm just saying that,

00:41:03.030 --> 00:41:04.780
that was just a complete sidebar

00:41:04.780 --> 00:41:07.450
but my point is is that
all our touch points

00:41:07.450 --> 00:41:10.330
were related to like the
Christmas Eve service

00:41:10.330 --> 00:41:14.970
and the things leading up to Christmas

00:41:14.970 --> 00:41:16.705
that we did as a church and
it was all very meaningful

00:41:16.705 --> 00:41:19.750
and it was all very personal and impactful

00:41:19.750 --> 00:41:21.943
and we were involved as a family.

00:41:23.075 --> 00:41:25.240
Well, let's move on to stage two, right?

00:41:25.240 --> 00:41:26.863
Because as we've established,

00:41:28.080 --> 00:41:31.350
that mentality and that
approach did not continue.

00:41:31.350 --> 00:41:34.100
For me, I struggled with doubt

00:41:34.100 --> 00:41:35.510
pretty much my entire adult life

00:41:35.510 --> 00:41:37.133
as it related to my Christian faith

00:41:37.133 --> 00:41:41.160
but probably about 15 years ago or so

00:41:41.160 --> 00:41:43.360
was when the doubts began to get

00:41:45.120 --> 00:41:47.290
kind of crippling to the point that

00:41:48.680 --> 00:41:53.680
engaging in like Bible
reading as an example,

00:41:53.870 --> 00:41:55.450
would inflame my doubts, right?

00:41:55.450 --> 00:42:00.100
So if I would go to the Bible
to have my doubts addressed,

00:42:00.100 --> 00:42:01.770
some of the other things that I had read

00:42:01.770 --> 00:42:04.190
about these particular
things would enter my mind

00:42:04.190 --> 00:42:05.120
and it became this thing

00:42:05.120 --> 00:42:08.010
where the more sensational the story,

00:42:08.010 --> 00:42:10.190
the more difficult it
was for me to believe

00:42:10.190 --> 00:42:12.810
and I feel like the Christmas story

00:42:12.810 --> 00:42:15.230
kind of brings together a lot
of different elements, right?

00:42:15.230 --> 00:42:16.920
So you've got some things that are,

00:42:16.920 --> 00:42:19.140
let's just be honest,
difficult to believe.

00:42:19.140 --> 00:42:22.670
Virgin birth, the idea that there's a star

00:42:22.670 --> 00:42:25.490
that is settling over
the town of Bethlehem

00:42:25.490 --> 00:42:27.630
that is leading the Wise Men to the town

00:42:27.630 --> 00:42:29.500
which seems to indicate

00:42:29.500 --> 00:42:32.260
that the authors didn't really understand

00:42:32.260 --> 00:42:34.470
the nature of stars and how
far away they actually are

00:42:34.470 --> 00:42:36.120
and how that's not how stars work

00:42:36.960 --> 00:42:38.330
or maybe it was a special star

00:42:38.330 --> 00:42:40.040
that was just happened for this.

00:42:40.040 --> 00:42:42.900
Listen, everything that
I'm gonna say right now,

00:42:42.900 --> 00:42:47.750
which is sort of like my doubts
that I have about the story,

00:42:47.750 --> 00:42:51.510
I am well aware that there are plenty

00:42:51.510 --> 00:42:54.640
of evangelical traditional
Christian explanations

00:42:54.640 --> 00:42:55.530
for all these things.

00:42:55.530 --> 00:42:57.080
I'm not discounting those.

00:42:57.080 --> 00:42:59.750
I'm just saying that for me,

00:42:59.750 --> 00:43:02.220
when I engage with the Christmas story

00:43:03.980 --> 00:43:05.910
from a historical perspective

00:43:05.910 --> 00:43:08.920
and some of the issues
that there are there

00:43:08.920 --> 00:43:11.620
related to like the Herod

00:43:11.620 --> 00:43:15.470
and the governor of Syria Quirinius

00:43:15.470 --> 00:43:16.840
or the census and these things

00:43:16.840 --> 00:43:18.530
that like you can kind
of call into question

00:43:18.530 --> 00:43:21.280
from a historical perspective
and the way that they line up

00:43:21.280 --> 00:43:24.400
or the fact that the Christmas story,

00:43:24.400 --> 00:43:28.497
the nativity story is kinda
added to Luke and Matthew

00:43:30.910 --> 00:43:33.290
but it's not in the earliest
gospel, the Book of Mark

00:43:33.290 --> 00:43:35.421
so it kinda lends itself to this idea

00:43:35.421 --> 00:43:38.820
that the legend of Jesus
was growing as time went by

00:43:38.820 --> 00:43:39.900
and so they were adding things

00:43:39.900 --> 00:43:41.220
like hey, let's add this story

00:43:41.220 --> 00:43:42.760
that shows how he fulfilled prophecy.

00:43:42.760 --> 00:43:45.160
Again, this is the secular
view of these things.

00:43:46.320 --> 00:43:48.840
And I began to see some of those answers

00:43:48.840 --> 00:43:52.840
and some of those explanations
to those difficult passages

00:43:52.840 --> 00:43:57.729
less as a good answer and
more as what felt like

00:43:57.729 --> 00:43:59.714
this seems more desperate, right?

00:43:59.714 --> 00:44:01.880
It's not satisfying to me

00:44:01.880 --> 00:44:05.310
and so when I would engage with the story,

00:44:05.310 --> 00:44:06.883
I would be thinking
about all those things.

00:44:06.883 --> 00:44:11.883
It's like I'm thinking about
the critical view of this story

00:44:14.100 --> 00:44:17.700
which is not a fun way to
engage with a story, right?

00:44:17.700 --> 00:44:22.540
And so, Christmas became a time

00:44:22.540 --> 00:44:25.140
where I was kind of two minds, right?

00:44:25.140 --> 00:44:27.170
There was some serious
cognitive dissonance going on

00:44:27.170 --> 00:44:29.030
because there was a real appreciation

00:44:29.030 --> 00:44:32.530
for the idea of Christmas and the idea

00:44:32.530 --> 00:44:35.000
that God would become one of us

00:44:35.000 --> 00:44:36.720
and would make that connection in a way

00:44:36.720 --> 00:44:38.480
that I had not seen demonstrated

00:44:38.480 --> 00:44:40.213
in any other faith system, right?

00:44:41.260 --> 00:44:43.130
And there was all the stuff
that went along with it

00:44:43.130 --> 00:44:45.020
and those songs that
we sang from that album

00:44:45.020 --> 00:44:46.120
that I can't remember.

00:44:48.220 --> 00:44:50.330
They were incredibly meaningful

00:44:50.330 --> 00:44:53.120
even in the middle of my
severe doubt about these things

00:44:53.120 --> 00:44:54.090
When I would read the story

00:44:54.090 --> 00:44:55.150
and these doubts would be inflamed,

00:44:55.150 --> 00:44:58.180
I could still move on
to singing the songs,

00:44:58.180 --> 00:45:01.090
singing the hymns, thinking about Jesus

00:45:01.090 --> 00:45:05.460
and it would be very
moving and very impactful

00:45:05.460 --> 00:45:09.500
but there was a few, a
good number of years there

00:45:09.500 --> 00:45:11.220
where the doubts were so strong

00:45:11.220 --> 00:45:14.800
that engaging with the story of Christmas

00:45:14.800 --> 00:45:17.623
was bit of a train wreck inside my mind.

00:45:18.960 --> 00:45:21.690
Yeah, I can understand what you're saying.

00:45:21.690 --> 00:45:25.760
I think in my process, Christmas
didn't bring up as much

00:45:25.760 --> 00:45:27.773
but it didn't,

00:45:28.720 --> 00:45:31.420
it wasn't as difficult
because there was more

00:45:31.420 --> 00:45:33.100
like the traditions that we had

00:45:33.100 --> 00:45:34.520
and the amount of family we had to visit,

00:45:34.520 --> 00:45:36.510
it was easier to get distracted

00:45:36.510 --> 00:45:41.510
and I felt like I tended to
focus on the expectations

00:45:41.660 --> 00:45:44.160
that I had placed on myself
to make sure that like

00:45:45.860 --> 00:45:47.940
we're remembering that
Jesus is the center of this

00:45:47.940 --> 00:45:49.850
and we're doing some
things and we do have some,

00:45:49.850 --> 00:45:51.550
we have the Advent calendar

00:45:51.550 --> 00:45:54.800
and we have traditions that
we're doing with the kids

00:45:56.970 --> 00:45:58.610
but it was easy personally, I think,

00:45:58.610 --> 00:46:00.530
as there were starting to be doubts

00:46:00.530 --> 00:46:03.450
for me just to go into distraction mode

00:46:03.450 --> 00:46:05.700
'cause there was so much
else going on anyway

00:46:06.750 --> 00:46:10.150
in terms of gifts and family
and food and everything else

00:46:10.150 --> 00:46:12.930
that is the secular reasons for the season

00:46:12.930 --> 00:46:14.680
that everybody falls back on.

00:46:14.680 --> 00:46:15.570
Right.

00:46:15.570 --> 00:46:18.080
I definitely remember
you talking about albums.

00:46:18.080 --> 00:46:20.210
At a certain point when I was,

00:46:20.210 --> 00:46:25.170
I mean our conversations were
pretty constant and so my,

00:46:25.170 --> 00:46:26.573
I was more resistant at first

00:46:26.573 --> 00:46:28.410
because I didn't wanna shake things up

00:46:28.410 --> 00:46:32.030
but as as I started to come
to grips with my own doubts

00:46:32.030 --> 00:46:36.818
and my own experience, I
remember at Christmas time,

00:46:36.818 --> 00:46:41.510
I would listen to Sufjan
Stevens' Christmas albums.

00:46:41.510 --> 00:46:42.450
Like for a couple of years,

00:46:42.450 --> 00:46:44.220
he would release one every year

00:46:44.220 --> 00:46:48.230
so there's like this four-disc
box set that as a family,

00:46:48.230 --> 00:46:51.450
it's still very much a
tradition for us to listen.

00:46:51.450 --> 00:46:54.740
This is the album that's
playing in our house constantly

00:46:54.740 --> 00:46:57.130
and I would recommend getting it

00:46:57.130 --> 00:46:59.370
if you're a fan of Sufjan's earlier stuff.

00:46:59.370 --> 00:47:00.540
His stuff now-

00:47:00.540 --> 00:47:01.373
I can't get into it.

00:47:01.373 --> 00:47:02.390
It's like-

00:47:02.390 --> 00:47:03.223
I tried to get into it-

00:47:03.223 --> 00:47:04.056
I don't know what you need to be

00:47:04.056 --> 00:47:05.190
under the influence of but-

00:47:05.190 --> 00:47:06.442
Well, it just went, it went-

00:47:06.442 --> 00:47:07.710
It's very electronic.

00:47:07.710 --> 00:47:09.230
He went electronic and
I'm just not into that.

00:47:09.230 --> 00:47:11.150
So this like acoustic homemade,

00:47:11.150 --> 00:47:14.460
feels like four track in his
own house like playing horns

00:47:14.460 --> 00:47:16.440
and having people who can't sing

00:47:16.440 --> 00:47:18.160
start to sing along with him and like-

00:47:18.160 --> 00:47:19.670
Yeah, it was awesome.

00:47:19.670 --> 00:47:24.663
It's really awesome but I
remember like thinking okay,

00:47:25.630 --> 00:47:29.150
if Sufjan, he's singing
these Christmas songs

00:47:29.150 --> 00:47:32.140
because he's got a Christian faith.

00:47:32.140 --> 00:47:36.840
I don't know his story but like
he's got this faith in Jesus

00:47:36.840 --> 00:47:39.690
and I don't know, I'm not
gonna put a label on him.

00:47:39.690 --> 00:47:42.400
I don't know what label he
is applies to himself if any

00:47:42.400 --> 00:47:45.450
or how that's changed over
the years but he made,

00:47:45.450 --> 00:47:48.800
he released meaningful Christmas music

00:47:48.800 --> 00:47:52.923
that was meaningful to me
and I thought this guy,

00:47:54.840 --> 00:47:59.020
he seems really progressive,
he's an artist, he's cool.

00:47:59.020 --> 00:48:01.510
I think maybe this is my future.

00:48:01.510 --> 00:48:03.460
Maybe there's something
in his relationship

00:48:03.460 --> 00:48:07.303
with Christmas and with Jesus
that like I could be like,

00:48:08.450 --> 00:48:10.940
I could take a cue from
Sufjan Stevens, you know?

00:48:10.940 --> 00:48:15.150
It's interesting, it's
like I'm not gonna read

00:48:15.150 --> 00:48:17.580
as many books as you, I'm
just gonna start listening

00:48:17.580 --> 00:48:19.042
to this guy and he
started saying if he can-

00:48:19.042 --> 00:48:21.400
The thing about music though,

00:48:21.400 --> 00:48:24.680
I think, this is an interesting point

00:48:24.680 --> 00:48:27.660
and I agree with it and
relate to it personally

00:48:27.660 --> 00:48:31.710
because music kinda transcends

00:48:33.150 --> 00:48:35.527
the intellectual doubts
that you might have

00:48:35.527 --> 00:48:37.870
and you're dealing with this
stuff that's kind of up here

00:48:37.870 --> 00:48:40.300
in your head space and there's a rational

00:48:40.300 --> 00:48:41.900
sort of battle that's happening?

00:48:43.266 --> 00:48:47.737
Music connects with your
soul in a different way

00:48:47.737 --> 00:48:51.280
and this is why I can
still listen, even today,

00:48:51.280 --> 00:48:53.563
I don't consider myself a Christian,

00:48:54.690 --> 00:48:58.090
I can listen to "Be Thou My Vision",

00:48:58.090 --> 00:49:01.260
one of my favorite hymns and cry.

00:49:01.260 --> 00:49:02.493
You know what I'm saying?

00:49:04.320 --> 00:49:07.410
So, yeah there's something that transcends

00:49:07.410 --> 00:49:12.320
that mental barrier in music
anyway so I think that was,

00:49:12.320 --> 00:49:14.750
and I think it keeps, honestly,

00:49:14.750 --> 00:49:17.656
it keeps people around for longer.

00:49:17.656 --> 00:49:22.170
There's something about
just singing together.

00:49:22.170 --> 00:49:26.448
I mean what other venue
do you have in your life

00:49:26.448 --> 00:49:29.370
where you go and you get together

00:49:29.370 --> 00:49:30.570
with a bunch of like-minded people

00:49:30.570 --> 00:49:33.520
and you sing songs that are
just the most passionate things

00:49:33.520 --> 00:49:35.210
you could possibly imagine?

00:49:35.210 --> 00:49:36.770
I mean that doesn't happen.

00:49:36.770 --> 00:49:39.745
Christians got that one down pretty good.

00:49:39.745 --> 00:49:43.130
I mean, the closest
thing that I can think of

00:49:43.130 --> 00:49:45.230
is when we went to our friend's house

00:49:45.230 --> 00:49:48.363
and we did the sing along last year.

00:49:49.380 --> 00:49:50.510
Oh, you didn't even come to that.

00:49:50.510 --> 00:49:51.830
You guys didn't come.

00:49:51.830 --> 00:49:53.580
You've totally missed out, man.

00:49:53.580 --> 00:49:54.787
Thank you.

00:49:54.787 --> 00:49:56.450
But like, we just sang.

00:49:56.450 --> 00:49:57.283
It was like singing together.

00:49:57.283 --> 00:49:58.420
I was like, man, singing-

00:49:58.420 --> 00:49:59.950
That was a Thanksgiving thing, I think.

00:49:59.950 --> 00:50:03.880
Singing together with other people,

00:50:03.880 --> 00:50:07.160
it's just something that
should happen in more places.

00:50:07.160 --> 00:50:09.220
But anyway, I digress.

00:50:09.220 --> 00:50:13.500
So there was that period

00:50:13.500 --> 00:50:15.610
where there was that
cognitive dissonance happening

00:50:15.610 --> 00:50:17.560
and it was just like I
can't engage with this

00:50:17.560 --> 00:50:20.430
but I love my family And I still love God

00:50:20.430 --> 00:50:22.630
and I'm trying to figure
all this stuff out.

00:50:23.840 --> 00:50:28.750
And then there was, again,
I told all the story,

00:50:28.750 --> 00:50:30.574
I don't remember the exact year.

00:50:30.574 --> 00:50:35.070
It was after we moved out here
when it became like official

00:50:35.070 --> 00:50:37.830
but still, more than several years ago

00:50:38.710 --> 00:50:40.540
where I was like okay, it's official,

00:50:40.540 --> 00:50:43.080
I don't believe this anymore.

00:50:43.080 --> 00:50:48.080
Like I cannot honestly
call myself a Christian.

00:50:48.460 --> 00:50:50.320
I'm not going to pursue this,

00:50:50.320 --> 00:50:51.750
I'm not going to engage with this,

00:50:51.750 --> 00:50:53.603
I'm not gonna go to church anymore.

00:50:54.960 --> 00:50:57.070
It wasn't that clean but there was a point

00:50:57.070 --> 00:50:59.940
in which that was who I became.

00:50:59.940 --> 00:51:01.470
But you still got Christmas rolling around

00:51:01.470 --> 00:51:02.880
every single year, right?

00:51:02.880 --> 00:51:04.510
And it's weird.

00:51:04.510 --> 00:51:06.890
It's weird when you have like,

00:51:06.890 --> 00:51:08.380
hey, we've been doing this every year

00:51:08.380 --> 00:51:13.380
and it's been just saturated in meaning.

00:51:13.480 --> 00:51:17.040
It's been saturated in the most

00:51:19.140 --> 00:51:24.140
sort of consequential
and important meaning

00:51:24.410 --> 00:51:26.460
that it could possibly have

00:51:26.460 --> 00:51:28.447
and now, you're just gonna
become one of those guys

00:51:28.447 --> 00:51:31.470
that's just getting through
the Christmas season

00:51:31.470 --> 00:51:34.790
on some good tidings from
the Christmas movies?

00:51:34.790 --> 00:51:39.170
For somebody who's had a really
deep spiritual experience,

00:51:42.010 --> 00:51:43.660
those Christmas movies,

00:51:43.660 --> 00:51:46.354
again, "Elf", great movie, doesn't cut it.

00:51:46.354 --> 00:51:49.610
If you've had that depth of experience-

00:51:49.610 --> 00:51:51.630
God is not a character.

00:51:51.630 --> 00:51:54.380
Will Ferrell is awesome but he is not God.

00:51:54.380 --> 00:51:58.810
And so, it's like you come to that time

00:51:58.810 --> 00:52:02.370
and there's this like, man,
the depth of experience

00:52:03.244 --> 00:52:06.570
and the depth that this
had associated with it

00:52:06.570 --> 00:52:08.100
that permeated my life personally

00:52:08.100 --> 00:52:12.030
but also permeated the lives
of my wives and children.

00:52:12.030 --> 00:52:13.142
Wife and-

00:52:13.142 --> 00:52:14.350
Watch out, man.

00:52:14.350 --> 00:52:17.010
My wife and children.

00:52:17.010 --> 00:52:20.173
Our family, that's an easier
way to say it, is not there.

00:52:21.298 --> 00:52:23.283
How do you engage with that?

00:52:23.283 --> 00:52:25.510
I think about the realization

00:52:25.510 --> 00:52:27.587
that that children's book that we had,

00:52:28.931 --> 00:52:32.740
it's like one year you pull
down the Christmas decorations

00:52:32.740 --> 00:52:33.850
and the Christmas books

00:52:33.850 --> 00:52:36.700
and like that book that Lily memorized

00:52:36.700 --> 00:52:40.480
that you read with Lincoln
some when he was younger

00:52:42.271 --> 00:52:45.870
that like you realize that
like you can't find it

00:52:45.870 --> 00:52:48.470
in the box anymore or I don't remember

00:52:48.470 --> 00:52:50.560
ever deciding to not
pull it out of the box

00:52:50.560 --> 00:52:53.820
or not to read it to
Lando but it's like yeah,

00:52:53.820 --> 00:52:57.234
it's just kinda like you
realize, you know what,

00:52:57.234 --> 00:53:01.393
Lando never read this
book or and I remember,

00:53:02.300 --> 00:53:04.870
I think I do remember Christy finding it

00:53:04.870 --> 00:53:07.690
and reading it to Lando at a young age

00:53:07.690 --> 00:53:11.730
and it was like, it wasn't
this communal experience

00:53:11.730 --> 00:53:13.170
that it was before because we were

00:53:13.170 --> 00:53:15.270
in this transitional time.

00:53:15.270 --> 00:53:18.150
And again, it kind of the Christmas season

00:53:18.150 --> 00:53:23.120
brought it into focus and part of it is

00:53:24.450 --> 00:53:25.283
while you look at the other,

00:53:25.283 --> 00:53:27.300
there's still a lot to be distracted by

00:53:27.300 --> 00:53:30.030
and we're still going home for Christmas

00:53:30.030 --> 00:53:32.837
and there's a lot of logistics involved

00:53:32.837 --> 00:53:35.573
and it was once we moved out here, so,

00:53:37.540 --> 00:53:41.110
it didn't feel like this painful moment.

00:53:41.110 --> 00:53:42.720
It was just like all of a sudden,

00:53:42.720 --> 00:53:44.670
you realize that book's not coming out

00:53:44.670 --> 00:53:47.013
of the box anymore, you know?

00:53:49.420 --> 00:53:53.113
And I do think, for me, that,

00:53:54.915 --> 00:53:56.310
and that still, even now,

00:53:56.310 --> 00:53:58.140
like I'm at a different phase

00:53:58.140 --> 00:54:02.610
than I was that was like
everything seemed to be changing

00:54:02.610 --> 00:54:05.420
much more rapidly in terms of my worldview

00:54:05.420 --> 00:54:10.420
and my belief paradigm in my allegiance

00:54:10.440 --> 00:54:13.430
to the evangelical worldview.

00:54:13.430 --> 00:54:16.360
You get to a point and
it's like you come to grips

00:54:16.360 --> 00:54:21.360
with that's not me anymore
and it's not changing as fast

00:54:21.830 --> 00:54:24.950
but there's still this residual

00:54:24.950 --> 00:54:28.133
in the back of my mind, I think.

00:54:31.680 --> 00:54:33.150
I guess I would just call it,

00:54:33.150 --> 00:54:34.980
there's an experience of guilt.

00:54:34.980 --> 00:54:37.197
It's like because there's this questions.

00:54:37.197 --> 00:54:38.720
It's like when you let,

00:54:38.720 --> 00:54:41.570
as you put it in your story,

00:54:41.570 --> 00:54:43.820
you jump ship you let go of something

00:54:43.820 --> 00:54:46.630
but you don't have anything
specific to grasp onto.

00:54:46.630 --> 00:54:48.720
It's like we're not now

00:54:51.040 --> 00:54:54.620
ascribing to some other
religious belief system.

00:54:54.620 --> 00:54:55.453
Well, and-

00:54:56.490 --> 00:55:00.660
So, I do think for me,

00:55:00.660 --> 00:55:02.393
there is a bit of,

00:55:03.520 --> 00:55:06.811
yeah, it's like did I
make the right decision?

00:55:06.811 --> 00:55:09.900
Did we as a family make a right decision?

00:55:09.900 --> 00:55:11.540
It's like, there's these little questions.

00:55:11.540 --> 00:55:16.540
It's like, I've tried my
best to embrace uncertainty

00:55:18.670 --> 00:55:22.170
as a positive but there's
still moments of struggle

00:55:22.170 --> 00:55:25.650
and I think it happens
more around the holidays

00:55:25.650 --> 00:55:27.520
when you realize that like something

00:55:27.520 --> 00:55:29.280
that was extremely meaningful

00:55:30.240 --> 00:55:33.610
in a practice that you
have with your first child

00:55:33.610 --> 00:55:36.980
is not part of what happens
with your third child

00:55:36.980 --> 00:55:38.963
and are are they missing out?

00:55:41.610 --> 00:55:43.360
Have we done them a disservice?

00:55:43.360 --> 00:55:45.990
And then I kinda have to rederive

00:55:45.990 --> 00:55:47.830
what brought me to this point

00:55:47.830 --> 00:55:52.640
and also, look at our
children and how tremendously

00:55:52.640 --> 00:55:56.400
fabulous they are and
how proud I am of them

00:55:56.400 --> 00:56:00.130
and start to just have this
reality check that like okay,

00:56:00.130 --> 00:56:04.810
these feelings of guilt or obligation,

00:56:04.810 --> 00:56:07.480
sometimes, I think I would describe it

00:56:07.480 --> 00:56:11.240
as I'm feeling judged by my former self

00:56:12.460 --> 00:56:15.050
because the position I'm in now in the way

00:56:15.050 --> 00:56:16.550
that I interact with Christmas

00:56:18.350 --> 00:56:21.467
is something that, again, I said earlier,

00:56:21.467 --> 00:56:25.150
I'd feel for people that they didn't have

00:56:25.150 --> 00:56:27.540
the depth of experience that I have

00:56:27.540 --> 00:56:29.090
and now, I'm in that position.

00:56:29.090 --> 00:56:33.530
Mm-hm, yeah, and I mean I
definitely relate to that.

00:56:33.530 --> 00:56:38.530
I mean, guilt is not really my,
that's not my thing as much.

00:56:39.430 --> 00:56:40.263
Always my thing.

00:56:40.263 --> 00:56:41.513
But there is a-

00:56:42.935 --> 00:56:45.670
And I'm not blaming it all
on evangelicalism either.

00:56:45.670 --> 00:56:50.490
It's a Link thing, it wasn't
created by the church.

00:56:50.490 --> 00:56:51.430
It was just how-

00:56:51.430 --> 00:56:52.263
Exacerbated by it.

00:56:52.263 --> 00:56:53.290
Yeah.

00:56:53.290 --> 00:56:55.830
I think that the, really
what you're getting at

00:56:55.830 --> 00:56:57.420
is one of the things you're doing

00:56:57.420 --> 00:57:00.236
is you're highlighting the
importance of religion, right?

00:57:00.236 --> 00:57:03.890
You're highlighting the
importance of a spiritual life

00:57:03.890 --> 00:57:08.890
and so, because if that meaning
is to be had from something,

00:57:10.300 --> 00:57:15.223
if you can find that meaning
and that purpose in something,

00:57:16.150 --> 00:57:19.760
well, that's one of the
reasons that religion exists.

00:57:19.760 --> 00:57:20.710
That's one of the really,

00:57:20.710 --> 00:57:24.430
that's the main reason that
people stick around for it

00:57:24.430 --> 00:57:27.750
even if they don't quite
believe it in full, right?

00:57:27.750 --> 00:57:30.130
If they have some doubts,
they're like but the alternative

00:57:30.130 --> 00:57:32.340
is just I don't believe anything

00:57:32.340 --> 00:57:34.710
and interesting that
you bring up that quote

00:57:34.710 --> 00:57:36.490
from my deconstruction story

00:57:36.490 --> 00:57:38.180
where I talked about jumping ship

00:57:38.180 --> 00:57:39.500
and it was a very dramatic line

00:57:39.500 --> 00:57:42.110
and it has been played
in many different videos

00:57:42.110 --> 00:57:44.683
that critiqued our deconstruction stories.

00:57:46.030 --> 00:57:50.830
There's one of my favorites is
one speaking of Kirk Cameron

00:57:50.830 --> 00:57:55.390
by Mr. Ray Comfort who works with Kirk

00:57:55.390 --> 00:57:58.371
and he kind of goes through

00:57:58.371 --> 00:58:01.460
and breaks down our story

00:58:01.460 --> 00:58:03.490
and play some very sentimental music

00:58:03.490 --> 00:58:08.490
and almost some like music that
sort of like impending doom

00:58:08.530 --> 00:58:09.960
the whole time as we tell our stories

00:58:09.960 --> 00:58:12.690
and many things are taken out of context.

00:58:12.690 --> 00:58:15.940
It's very entertaining
but one of the things

00:58:15.940 --> 00:58:17.810
is that line about I jumped ship

00:58:17.810 --> 00:58:20.737
and I took my wife and my children with me

00:58:20.737 --> 00:58:22.220
and it's just like, people quote,

00:58:22.220 --> 00:58:24.590
like it's so sad, he took his
wife and his children with me.

00:58:24.590 --> 00:58:26.983
I think I regret saying,

00:58:26.983 --> 00:58:30.610
it was a little bit of
a dramatic thing to say.

00:58:30.610 --> 00:58:34.400
I regret saying it because
I think the better analogy

00:58:34.400 --> 00:58:36.900
is I jumped out of a ship

00:58:36.900 --> 00:58:39.260
and there's not another ship like that

00:58:39.260 --> 00:58:40.890
that you're jumping into, right?

00:58:40.890 --> 00:58:43.900
But it doesn't mean that
you have no meaning,

00:58:43.900 --> 00:58:47.000
you have no purpose and you
have no principles in your life.

00:58:47.000 --> 00:58:49.200
Those those things are still intact.

00:58:49.200 --> 00:58:50.400
The source and the-
It doesn't mean

00:58:50.400 --> 00:58:51.910
that you're drowning.

00:58:51.910 --> 00:58:54.240
Yeah, the source and the
philosophical foundation

00:58:54.240 --> 00:58:56.720
of those things is coming
from a different place

00:58:56.720 --> 00:58:59.550
and it may be a place that
you, as a Christian philosopher

00:58:59.550 --> 00:59:03.750
may say it is illegitimate,
I would disagree.

00:59:03.750 --> 00:59:05.660
I'm just saying that like it
isn't like I've been swimming

00:59:05.660 --> 00:59:09.420
in this ocean of uncertainty
and my family is going nuts

00:59:09.420 --> 00:59:12.060
but that's how it was interpreted.

00:59:12.060 --> 00:59:16.710
But I mean I agree with what you're saying

00:59:16.710 --> 00:59:18.850
in the sense that it's like, all right,

00:59:18.850 --> 00:59:21.400
you approach this and there's,

00:59:21.400 --> 00:59:23.820
the puzzle pieces are in place.

00:59:23.820 --> 00:59:25.990
Like every time you come
around to Christmas,

00:59:25.990 --> 00:59:27.320
it's just like we have a puzzle,

00:59:27.320 --> 00:59:28.710
we know where the pieces go,

00:59:28.710 --> 00:59:31.420
we can sell our kids This is how it works

00:59:31.420 --> 00:59:33.510
and then all of a sudden,

00:59:33.510 --> 00:59:37.310
you come to the holiday and
it's like the puzzle doesn't,

00:59:37.310 --> 00:59:40.507
can't fit together in a
very satisfying way anymore

00:59:40.507 --> 00:59:41.720
and so you don't-

00:59:41.720 --> 00:59:44.589
The central assertion was
don't forget what matters most.

00:59:44.589 --> 00:59:45.422
Yeah.

00:59:45.422 --> 00:59:48.290
That was our experience in phase one.

00:59:48.290 --> 00:59:49.123
Yeah.

00:59:49.123 --> 00:59:51.800
And then in the doubting phase,

00:59:51.800 --> 00:59:53.250
well, now, we're talking
about phase three now.

00:59:53.250 --> 00:59:54.900
We're still in phase three.

00:59:54.900 --> 00:59:58.595
Okay, phase three of you know what,

00:59:58.595 --> 01:00:01.430
I haven't replaced that matters most

01:00:01.430 --> 01:00:03.070
with something else specifically

01:00:03.070 --> 01:00:05.770
but we're just getting through this

01:00:05.770 --> 01:00:10.693
and honestly, I'm not suffering,
my family is not suffering.

01:00:12.503 --> 01:00:14.590
It's not a horrible experience.

01:00:14.590 --> 01:00:15.550
But you're hearing the echoes

01:00:15.550 --> 01:00:17.570
of the old Link saying-
But I'm hearing echoes, yes.

01:00:17.570 --> 01:00:19.900
There is no meaning here.

01:00:19.900 --> 01:00:21.630
This is pointless.

01:00:21.630 --> 01:00:23.410
The things that we would
have thought about people

01:00:23.410 --> 01:00:25.546
who weren't Christians before
when we were Christians

01:00:25.546 --> 01:00:27.610
and you find yourself in
it and you're like, man,

01:00:27.610 --> 01:00:30.940
like I still really love my wife.

01:00:30.940 --> 01:00:32.443
I still really love my family.

01:00:33.880 --> 01:00:36.410
We stand for very similar things.

01:00:36.410 --> 01:00:38.210
We're not different people

01:00:38.210 --> 01:00:42.470
but we don't know how
to reconcile this story

01:00:42.470 --> 01:00:43.590
in the same way

01:00:43.590 --> 01:00:47.960
and so you find yourself
becoming the secular person

01:00:47.960 --> 01:00:51.230
that you felt sorry for and you're like-

01:00:51.230 --> 01:00:52.739
It's about the food, the decorations.

01:00:52.739 --> 01:00:55.470
I'm getting through Christmas
on the accoutrement.

01:00:55.470 --> 01:00:59.570
Service and family and love.

01:00:59.570 --> 01:01:02.670
But in an effort to
transition into stage four,

01:01:02.670 --> 01:01:06.330
which is which I don't
like saying stage four

01:01:06.330 --> 01:01:07.780
'cause it sounds like cancer.

01:01:10.240 --> 01:01:11.203
Phase four.

01:01:13.979 --> 01:01:15.770
I actually personally,

01:01:15.770 --> 01:01:17.190
again, this is not prescriptive,

01:01:17.190 --> 01:01:18.610
I'm not saying this for anybody else.

01:01:18.610 --> 01:01:19.540
This is for me.

01:01:19.540 --> 01:01:21.800
I actually do find phase three

01:01:21.800 --> 01:01:24.360
to be inadequate for me, personally.

01:01:24.360 --> 01:01:29.290
So the idea that Christmas
is just about those things,

01:01:29.290 --> 01:01:32.250
just about the gift the
giving and the receiving

01:01:32.250 --> 01:01:37.250
and the good tidings and
great joy unrelated to Jesus,

01:01:37.610 --> 01:01:39.360
just the secular side of things,

01:01:39.360 --> 01:01:42.373
just watching "Elf" or seeing
Tim Allen be Santa again,

01:01:43.480 --> 01:01:46.350
I do find those things to be inadequate.

01:01:46.350 --> 01:01:50.720
Like I didn't wanna be
stuck at phase three.

01:01:50.720 --> 01:01:55.170
In other words, I didn't want to become

01:01:55.170 --> 01:02:00.170
a completely non-spiritual person

01:02:01.220 --> 01:02:05.010
who was like that's all just mumbo-jumbo

01:02:05.010 --> 01:02:10.010
and I'm gonna just build my
life on rationality completely

01:02:10.400 --> 01:02:12.140
and it's just a natural existence

01:02:12.140 --> 01:02:13.490
and that's it and that's,

01:02:13.490 --> 01:02:15.350
now, lots of people have done that.

01:02:15.350 --> 01:02:16.820
More power to you if that works for you.

01:02:16.820 --> 01:02:17.653
For me-

01:02:17.653 --> 01:02:20.870
And by the way, people
have to other religions

01:02:20.870 --> 01:02:23.750
and then they have, so
then they have new holidays

01:02:23.750 --> 01:02:27.130
that they don't have to come to grips

01:02:27.130 --> 01:02:29.960
with Christmas on other terms,
they have other holidays

01:02:29.960 --> 01:02:33.550
that are in place of it that
have depth of meaning that-

01:02:33.550 --> 01:02:34.735
But they're not as good as Christmas.

01:02:36.780 --> 01:02:37.863
I'm just kidding.

01:02:39.910 --> 01:02:42.840
But something interesting
has happened to me

01:02:44.490 --> 01:02:45.840
and I think, I mean it's been happening

01:02:45.840 --> 01:02:46.790
over the past few years.

01:02:46.790 --> 01:02:50.760
This is not super new but
when we broke the seal

01:02:50.760 --> 01:02:52.400
earlier this year.

01:02:52.400 --> 01:02:53.780
Boy, when we were telling those stories

01:02:53.780 --> 01:02:54.650
about our deconstruction,

01:02:54.650 --> 01:02:56.666
we had no idea what the
hell 2020 was gonna bring.

01:02:56.666 --> 01:02:59.550
We had no idea that people
were gonna no longer care

01:02:59.550 --> 01:03:01.400
about our deconstruction story

01:03:01.400 --> 01:03:04.700
as soon as they found out about COVID-19.

01:03:04.700 --> 01:03:05.900
Maybe it was a blessing.

01:03:06.934 --> 01:03:08.023
I think it was a blessing.

01:03:08.023 --> 01:03:09.170
From that perspective.

01:03:09.170 --> 01:03:11.663
It's not a blessing for
the world by any means.

01:03:14.320 --> 01:03:17.420
but we had a really interesting,

01:03:17.420 --> 01:03:18.730
I'm using the word interesting a lot

01:03:18.730 --> 01:03:21.080
and I hate the word
interesting so I apologize.

01:03:22.750 --> 01:03:27.310
We had a unique perspective on

01:03:29.200 --> 01:03:31.980
the way that we would
approach our past faith

01:03:31.980 --> 01:03:33.880
for the bulk of our career, right?

01:03:33.880 --> 01:03:36.450
We're kind of a like a
little bit embarrassment

01:03:36.450 --> 01:03:39.630
about how serious we were
and how far we went in

01:03:39.630 --> 01:03:41.310
and the fact that we were missionaries.

01:03:41.310 --> 01:03:43.330
I mean not necessarily embarrassment

01:03:43.330 --> 01:03:45.840
but like this is gonna
be difficult to explain

01:03:45.840 --> 01:03:47.810
and I'm going to say where I'm at now

01:03:47.810 --> 01:03:51.223
and so there was almost
an avoidance, a secrecy.

01:03:52.130 --> 01:03:54.330
I'm sure some of you who have
been fans for a long time

01:03:54.330 --> 01:03:55.804
could sense that.

01:03:55.804 --> 01:03:58.370
They're like, "Oh, they
don't talk about their past."

01:03:58.370 --> 01:04:00.890
And I think that it
actually influenced the way

01:04:00.890 --> 01:04:03.237
that I dealt with it personally.

01:04:03.237 --> 01:04:06.380
It inhibited my own personal freedom

01:04:06.380 --> 01:04:08.260
to explore spiritual things

01:04:08.260 --> 01:04:09.927
because I had such a
weird relationship with it

01:04:09.927 --> 01:04:14.927
and I was this public
figure that had this past

01:04:15.210 --> 01:04:17.000
that I kind of couldn't explain

01:04:17.000 --> 01:04:18.910
and didn't wanna go into the details of

01:04:18.910 --> 01:04:22.500
but when we made the
decision to tell the story

01:04:22.500 --> 01:04:24.563
in its entirety without apology,

01:04:25.670 --> 01:04:27.753
it broke a seal for me, personally.

01:04:28.750 --> 01:04:32.140
And it what it did is it kinda,

01:04:32.140 --> 01:04:35.620
it was like something
within me got the okay

01:04:35.620 --> 01:04:38.630
to be like all right, you can move on now.

01:04:38.630 --> 01:04:40.770
You don't have to be in this place.

01:04:40.770 --> 01:04:42.920
This is just a guy who
used to be a Christian

01:04:42.920 --> 01:04:44.970
and doesn't believe that stuff anymore

01:04:44.970 --> 01:04:46.450
and that's who you are,

01:04:46.450 --> 01:04:47.630
you can actually move forward

01:04:47.630 --> 01:04:50.703
to whatever's next for you
from a spiritual perspective.

01:04:52.430 --> 01:04:55.307
And one of the things that has happened

01:04:55.307 --> 01:04:57.963
and this is, I don't know where,

01:04:58.800 --> 01:05:01.820
I don't know exactly where it's
all going spiritually for me

01:05:01.820 --> 01:05:03.720
but I said to him when I told my story

01:05:03.720 --> 01:05:05.750
that I had an openness and I did.

01:05:05.750 --> 01:05:07.265
I have an openness, I did

01:05:07.265 --> 01:05:11.450
and I do currently have an
openness towards spiritual things

01:05:12.600 --> 01:05:14.280
and one of the interesting things that,

01:05:14.280 --> 01:05:17.370
interesting again, one of
the things that has happened

01:05:17.370 --> 01:05:21.970
is sort of a reengaging
with the person of Jesus

01:05:23.130 --> 01:05:26.471
in a completely different way and that is

01:05:26.471 --> 01:05:30.120
I used to think about anything that,

01:05:30.120 --> 01:05:32.010
if I go to the Bible and
I would read something

01:05:32.010 --> 01:05:34.310
that Jesus said, again,
I was sort of overwhelmed

01:05:34.310 --> 01:05:38.100
with well, let's bring
in the critical lens,

01:05:38.100 --> 01:05:39.340
let's bring in the perspective

01:05:39.340 --> 01:05:42.050
of the Jesus seminar onto this text.

01:05:42.050 --> 01:05:44.603
That's not a fun way to
interact with Jesus, right?

01:05:46.010 --> 01:05:48.320
Or a particularly useful way, personally,

01:05:48.320 --> 01:05:51.120
when it comes to like your
own personal edification.

01:05:51.120 --> 01:05:55.270
There's been a couple of good
books that I've read this year

01:05:55.270 --> 01:05:57.220
that I'm not gonna go into

01:05:57.220 --> 01:06:00.340
but have sort of changed my perspective

01:06:00.340 --> 01:06:03.210
on how I can engage with Jesus,

01:06:03.210 --> 01:06:06.050
not as someone who

01:06:06.050 --> 01:06:11.050
is God in the flesh

01:06:11.340 --> 01:06:14.070
that is the only way to be
reconciled with a vengeful God

01:06:14.070 --> 01:06:15.823
who has to punish somebody.

01:06:16.920 --> 01:06:20.040
I'm not holding on to any of the old stuff

01:06:21.230 --> 01:06:23.630
but just looking at
what Jesus said and did

01:06:23.630 --> 01:06:26.660
as a spiritual teacher and being like

01:06:26.660 --> 01:06:28.943
there's a lot there, right?

01:06:29.907 --> 01:06:34.350
And even engaging in the Christmas story,

01:06:34.350 --> 01:06:36.530
not with a preoccupation
about whether or not

01:06:36.530 --> 01:06:41.200
it's historically true or based in fact

01:06:41.200 --> 01:06:43.970
but is there a truth there to be gleaned?

01:06:43.970 --> 01:06:46.420
Is there something that
you and your family

01:06:46.420 --> 01:06:48.950
can actually get from interacting with it?

01:06:48.950 --> 01:06:52.140
Taking it at face value
without getting into this game

01:06:52.140 --> 01:06:54.510
of trying to figure out
whether it's real or not,

01:06:54.510 --> 01:06:56.800
which is a little bit ironic

01:06:56.800 --> 01:06:58.970
because if you think about
the stories that Jesus,

01:06:58.970 --> 01:07:01.830
I mean, first of all Jesus
taught in parable, right?

01:07:01.830 --> 01:07:06.343
He taught in story, he told
stories, he made analogies.

01:07:07.180 --> 01:07:12.180
And the fact that no one is
ever recorded in the Bible

01:07:13.190 --> 01:07:15.930
as responding to one of
the stories that he told

01:07:15.930 --> 01:07:19.003
with but did that really happen?

01:07:20.000 --> 01:07:21.030
Okay, yeah.

01:07:21.030 --> 01:07:22.860
No one was like, "But hold on, hold on.

01:07:22.860 --> 01:07:25.200
This thing with the Samaritan,
did that really happen?

01:07:25.200 --> 01:07:26.150
Did it happen last week?

01:07:26.150 --> 01:07:27.250
Did you see it happen?

01:07:27.250 --> 01:07:30.937
'Cause if you didn't see it
happen, I don't believe it."

01:07:32.290 --> 01:07:37.290
His point was is that
truth is not, I think,

01:07:40.350 --> 01:07:42.980
truth is not something
that is just contained

01:07:42.980 --> 01:07:47.170
in this factually historical

01:07:48.830 --> 01:07:52.963
verifiable vessel, right?

01:07:54.000 --> 01:07:58.480
Truth comes in a lot of different
forms and I can listen to,

01:07:58.480 --> 01:08:00.820
I can watch a movie, right?

01:08:00.820 --> 01:08:04.493
I can watch a movie that is
from beginning to end, fiction

01:08:04.493 --> 01:08:06.680
and still find truth in it.

01:08:06.680 --> 01:08:08.870
And I'm not, listen, I'm not saying okay,

01:08:08.870 --> 01:08:10.480
the only way I can engage
with the Christmas stories

01:08:10.480 --> 01:08:13.430
by just saying it's a
fairy tale and that's it

01:08:13.430 --> 01:08:15.100
but I'm saying that if I quit,

01:08:15.100 --> 01:08:17.030
if I turn that part of my brain off

01:08:17.030 --> 01:08:20.260
that is just constantly trying to judge

01:08:20.260 --> 01:08:23.160
whether or not Jesus actually said this

01:08:23.160 --> 01:08:25.080
or whether or not this actually happened,

01:08:25.080 --> 01:08:27.690
whether or not somebody was
a virgin and got pregnant

01:08:27.690 --> 01:08:30.740
and we're just like, let's
set those things aside

01:08:30.740 --> 01:08:33.020
because I'm not gonna
reconcile those things.

01:08:33.020 --> 01:08:35.180
I mean I have a very strong opinion

01:08:35.180 --> 01:08:38.760
about some of those things
and some very strong doubts

01:08:38.760 --> 01:08:41.340
but is there a story to be heard there?

01:08:41.340 --> 01:08:42.900
Is there a lesson to be learned there?

01:08:42.900 --> 01:08:45.223
Is there a truth within this?

01:08:48.330 --> 01:08:53.200
And I think that that is very
freeing for me personally.

01:08:53.200 --> 01:08:55.280
Does that translate into

01:08:55.280 --> 01:08:57.520
like something going into stocking?

01:08:57.520 --> 01:09:00.130
I mean, is there a practical,

01:09:00.130 --> 01:09:02.892
there doesn't have to
be for like Christmas

01:09:02.892 --> 01:09:05.343
and maybe this is,

01:09:07.790 --> 01:09:10.850
maybe my question is
revealing about my own issue

01:09:10.850 --> 01:09:12.460
which I can get into but,

01:09:12.460 --> 01:09:14.160
so maybe it's not a fair question.

01:09:15.080 --> 01:09:16.390
Do you even think about it that way?

01:09:16.390 --> 01:09:17.223
Like-

01:09:17.223 --> 01:09:18.500
No, it's not really what I'm-

01:09:18.500 --> 01:09:20.860
Are you saying at Christmas time,

01:09:20.860 --> 01:09:23.090
you're reflecting on the story

01:09:23.090 --> 01:09:28.090
but you're doing it in a way
that it can be edifying to you,

01:09:28.460 --> 01:09:30.760
your interaction with Jesus
can be edifying for you

01:09:30.760 --> 01:09:34.250
as opposed to it being something
that you're trying to judge

01:09:34.250 --> 01:09:35.360
or tear something down?

01:09:35.360 --> 01:09:36.193
Yeah, that.

01:09:36.193 --> 01:09:40.750
Because you're either not
gonna interact with Jesus

01:09:43.430 --> 01:09:44.420
at Christmas time

01:09:45.620 --> 01:09:48.930
or you're gonna have
a negative interaction

01:09:48.930 --> 01:09:50.550
or now, you're trying to say

01:09:50.550 --> 01:09:53.150
I'm gonna have the positive interaction

01:09:53.150 --> 01:09:56.210
that I'm able to have And I'm actually,

01:09:56.210 --> 01:09:58.960
I'm at a point where I can have that

01:09:58.960 --> 01:10:00.773
and that's what I'm gonna have.

01:10:01.756 --> 01:10:04.373
Well, and I think some people would say,

01:10:05.590 --> 01:10:07.310
guys, this is where,

01:10:07.310 --> 01:10:12.310
this is where the
enlightenment screwed things up

01:10:12.660 --> 01:10:14.990
because if you go back
to pre-enlightenment

01:10:14.990 --> 01:10:16.960
and pre sort of modern
thinking about things

01:10:16.960 --> 01:10:18.923
and pre-rational thought about things,

01:10:20.100 --> 01:10:23.760
this is how people engaged
with the stories of Jesus.

01:10:23.760 --> 01:10:25.150
There was not a preoccupation

01:10:25.150 --> 01:10:26.909
with whether or not these
things happen or not.

01:10:26.909 --> 01:10:31.010
There wasn't this
tendency to want to verify

01:10:31.010 --> 01:10:33.190
and completely wrap your
mind around these things

01:10:33.190 --> 01:10:35.470
but there was a spiritual
interaction with them

01:10:35.470 --> 01:10:37.410
and I believe that there
are still many Christians

01:10:37.410 --> 01:10:38.243
who would say hey guys,

01:10:38.243 --> 01:10:41.440
this is what my faith
looks like right now.

01:10:41.440 --> 01:10:43.110
Yeah, I guess

01:10:44.950 --> 01:10:46.093
my old mindset creeps in

01:10:46.093 --> 01:10:48.700
because it's like the
way I interacted with it

01:10:48.700 --> 01:10:53.700
was God became human in order
to save us from ourselves.

01:10:54.150 --> 01:10:55.121
Well, even that, okay?

01:10:55.121 --> 01:10:59.200
Right, so when we look
at the story of Christmas

01:10:59.200 --> 01:11:00.823
from a Christian perspective,

01:11:03.000 --> 01:11:06.780
you're right, it's God emptying himself,

01:11:06.780 --> 01:11:11.113
becoming a baby, again, I
don't know how this works.

01:11:12.240 --> 01:11:13.810
I don't actually believe
that's what was happening

01:11:13.810 --> 01:11:16.663
but according to the
story, becomes a baby,

01:11:17.918 --> 01:11:22.918
becomes sort of the complete
100% God, 100% human

01:11:23.210 --> 01:11:26.270
that then is the only
sacrifice that can be made

01:11:26.270 --> 01:11:29.190
in order to reconcile everyone

01:11:29.190 --> 01:11:32.540
who will call on the name
of the Lord to God, right?

01:11:32.540 --> 01:11:35.150
But isn't there a different way to,

01:11:35.150 --> 01:11:36.950
isn't there something else to appreciate

01:11:36.950 --> 01:11:38.509
without that having to be true, right?

01:11:38.509 --> 01:11:41.333
For instance, since you
mentioned this exact thing

01:11:41.333 --> 01:11:43.433
because I was thinking about this earlier.

01:11:45.000 --> 01:11:46.650
I don't know the nature of God.

01:11:46.650 --> 01:11:50.210
I don't necessarily know
anyone can understand,

01:11:50.210 --> 01:11:54.290
grasp or know or talk about
in a understandable way

01:11:54.290 --> 01:11:55.170
the nature of God.

01:11:55.170 --> 01:11:58.373
I think that there are, if there is a God,

01:12:00.530 --> 01:12:02.948
there's probably an experience of that God

01:12:02.948 --> 01:12:06.370
is somewhat ineffable, meaning
you cannot communicate it

01:12:06.370 --> 01:12:08.260
in a way that would make sense

01:12:08.260 --> 01:12:10.040
because it's happening
in a different place

01:12:10.040 --> 01:12:12.040
on a different level in a different way

01:12:12.040 --> 01:12:14.563
than human language can express.

01:12:16.030 --> 01:12:21.030
But the idea that God
would want to be so close

01:12:23.210 --> 01:12:26.600
and so involved and so
much a part of humanity

01:12:28.620 --> 01:12:33.530
that he would become one of
us is a beautiful concept

01:12:33.530 --> 01:12:36.270
that makes me think
about the nature of God

01:12:36.270 --> 01:12:38.630
in an open and edifying way.

01:12:38.630 --> 01:12:39.500
Does that make sense?

01:12:39.500 --> 01:12:43.290
It doesn't have to have
happened as described

01:12:43.290 --> 01:12:45.890
for me to be like that,

01:12:45.890 --> 01:12:47.490
in the way, I'm glad
we talked about music.

01:12:47.490 --> 01:12:49.722
I didn't know that's what's gonna happen

01:12:49.722 --> 01:12:53.770
but a song resonates with you.

01:12:53.770 --> 01:12:54.603
There's something about-

01:12:54.603 --> 01:12:55.436
In a soul level.

01:12:55.436 --> 01:12:58.380
There's something about
music that you connect with

01:12:58.380 --> 01:13:00.160
and you wouldn't say that song is true

01:13:00.160 --> 01:13:03.340
and that song is false but
you would be like this song,

01:13:03.340 --> 01:13:07.010
I feel like I begin to actually

01:13:08.190 --> 01:13:10.790
resonate and synchronize with this music

01:13:10.790 --> 01:13:13.940
because it connects with
my soul and this doesn't.

01:13:13.940 --> 01:13:18.260
I feel like that can
happen with a story as well

01:13:18.260 --> 01:13:21.450
and so, for me, there
are elements of that idea

01:13:21.450 --> 01:13:23.007
because I mean, if anything,

01:13:23.007 --> 01:13:26.410
the concept of God being in everything

01:13:26.410 --> 01:13:29.255
and God being available within someone,

01:13:29.255 --> 01:13:33.720
the universe, the fabric of the universe

01:13:33.720 --> 01:13:35.900
being whatever you wanna call it,

01:13:35.900 --> 01:13:37.890
that's something that's
still very intriguing to me

01:13:37.890 --> 01:13:40.090
that I wanna be open to
and I wanna lean into

01:13:40.090 --> 01:13:42.500
and I feel like I can find
that in the story of Christmas.

01:13:42.500 --> 01:13:43.333
That's all I'm saying.

01:13:43.333 --> 01:13:48.333
I think our former selves
would be saying right now,

01:13:48.360 --> 01:13:50.120
I mean, you just can't,

01:13:50.120 --> 01:13:54.350
you can't invent, you
can't just invent the terms

01:13:54.350 --> 01:13:56.120
with which you interact with Jesus.

01:13:56.120 --> 01:14:00.260
I mean, you're missing the point.

01:14:00.260 --> 01:14:03.500
You're just inventing a new
way to interact with Jesus

01:14:03.500 --> 01:14:05.037
that is just picking and
choosing what you want

01:14:05.037 --> 01:14:07.650
that's gonna be inspirational for you.

01:14:07.650 --> 01:14:10.571
I think that's what our former selves

01:14:10.571 --> 01:14:11.453
would've said.
Of course,

01:14:11.453 --> 01:14:12.759
that's what I would've said.

01:14:12.759 --> 01:14:14.426
But I don't think,

01:14:15.957 --> 01:14:18.430
and it doesn't matter
what anybody's saying.

01:14:18.430 --> 01:14:22.350
I think for you, you're making a decision

01:14:22.350 --> 01:14:25.386
because I do think that
the decision has been,

01:14:25.386 --> 01:14:29.730
is there gonna be any
interaction with Jesus, you know?

